      "title": "General Guidance on Authentication Loops and SSO Redirect Failures",
      "content_summary": "Troubleshooting steps for resolving HTTP 401 errors, login loops, and SSO redirect failures caused by identity provider issues or expired certificates.",
      "content_body": "Authentication loops and HTTP 401 errors often stem from identity provider outages, expired certificates, or unsupported configurations within MFA Manager or Help Center. When SSO redirect loops or premature session expirations occur, check the certificate expiration dates first and renew if necessary. If the issue persists, verify that the current setup is supported and perform a token/session reset to clear stale state. For complex vendor-side outages, escalate to the identity provider vendor immediately. Ensure that users are educated on password reset link expiration policies to prevent unnecessary lockouts."
